docs {
  Hypertube API - request collection with assertions.

  Run it top to bottom (`make test-api` or the Bruno runner): the requests
  are numbered and share runtime variables (runId, adaId, token). Every run
  registers a fresh user, so re-running never hits the 409 on its own data.

  Requests 26 to 34 walk a session through login, refresh, reuse of a rotated
  token and logout (ADR-0011) and wait 15 s once, to get out of the 10 s
  tolerance for a rotated token: a run takes about 20 s.

  Rate limits: POST /users is capped at 10 per hour per IP and a run uses 4.
  The dev stack multiplies every limit by THROTTLE_LIMIT_MULTIPLIER (set in
  .env, see .env.example) so repeated runs don't hit 429. With the default of
  1, wait or restart the backend after 3 runs.

  The `local` environment builds baseUrl from HYPERTUBE_HTTPS_PORT: the app is
  only reachable through the edge proxy (https://localhost:<port>/api, a
  self-signed certificate, so the CLI runs with --insecure). `make test-api`
  passes the port from the repo .env.

  Full endpoint reference: /api-docs on the backend (Swagger UI)
}

script:pre-request {
  // Bruno keeps a cookie jar across requests: the refresh cookie a login sets
  // would ride along on every later request and make "no cookie" impossible.
  // Start each request with an empty jar; a request that needs a cookie sets it
  // explicitly in its headers.
  await bru.cookies.clear();
}
